course: dictionary
lesson: 14096
title: Memorisation
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Memorisation means learning something so well that you can remember it exactly, such as a poem, a spelling or a times table. «We practise memorisation every Monday with our spelling list.» Practise and spelling list are your clues: memorisation is learning the words so you can recall them exactly.
explain: Another way to say it is learning by heart. «Our class learnt the poem by memorisation, so we could say it without the book.» Without the book tells you the poem was in your head, not on the page.
explain: Teachers say memorisation is useful, but it is not enough on its own. «Do not just memorise the rule; understand why it works.» Knowing a fact is good, but knowing why it is true is even better, because then you can use it in new questions.
fact: Memorisation means learning something so you can remember it exactly.
fact: Learning by heart means the same as memorisation.
fact: Rote memorisation means learning by repeating something again and again, even when you do not understand it yet.
fact: Memorisation techniques are tricks that help you remember, such as rhymes, pictures or saying facts out loud.
fact: Understanding why something is true helps you remember it and use it in new situations.
exercise: «We practise memorisation of our spellings every week.» What is memorisation? | Drawing pictures of a story | *Learning something so well you can remember it exactly | Reading a book quickly | Forgetting words on purpose
exercise: Mrs Patel says, «Memorisation of the times tables helps you answer fast.» What does memorisation help you do? | Draw maps of the classroom | *Remember facts exactly so you can answer quickly | Ask questions about the teacher | Read without any words
exercise: Which phrase means learning by repeating something until it sticks, even without understanding it? | Group work | Story writing | Mental arithmetic | *Rote memorisation
test: «The class learnt their poem by memorisation.» What does this sentence tell us? | The class read the poem once | The class forgot the poem | *The class learnt the poem by heart | The class wrote their own poem
test: Ravi says memorisation is useless, you only need to understand. What is a good answer? | Memorisation means drawing pictures | Never learn anything by heart | *Memorisation helps, but understanding why something is true matters too | Memorisation is the only thing that matters
exam: Which is the best memorisation technique? | *Saying facts out loud and repeating them with a rhyme | Skipping every fact that is hard | Closing your eyes and hoping | Never looking at the words again
